      },
      "lineNbr": 365,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-02T23:24:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you please use `SkSpan srcRow` to view into `rust::Slice... imageData`?  `base::span` has more checks, but even `SkSpan` has some `SkUNREACHABLE` assertions.  And in general, operating on ptr+size together seems nice and more robust than operating on ptr and size somewhat separately.\n\nThis may also mean that we don\u0027t need `y` multiplication (e.g. `y * dstRowStride`) and therefore don\u0027t even need to think about whether this multiplication could possibly overflow (I think it can\u0027t, but not thinking about it would be even nicer).\n\n------------------------------\n\n`dst` is a raw pointer in some public APIs of `SkCodec`, but we do store it as `SkSpan` in `state.fDecodingDstInfo.fDst`, so I think it would also be nice to represent `dstRow` as `SkSpan`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 364,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 365,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "24152c66c06bb44ec97219790b861dfac9193c29",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c89f8b8_fa2009b6",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_bmp/decoder/impl/SkBmpRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 506,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-02T23:24:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I expected that when Rust decodes N first rows, then those rows would be \"immediately\" available to the Skia client (e.g. swizzled + reported via `rowsDecodedPtr`).\n\nAs-is, it seems that the full BMP needs to be received before *any* pixels can be rendered.  Maybe I missed something?\n\nPS. Thank you for adding the `Codec_Bmp_Rust_IncrementalDecode_ProgressiveStream` test.  I think this test should verify the initial rows when `incrementalDecode` returns `kIncompleteInput` (around new line 530-568 in `SkBmpRustDecoderTest.cpp`).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 506,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "24152c66c06bb44ec97219790b861dfac9193c29",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae12a7e9_adbcf0b7",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_bmp/decoder/impl/SkBmpRustCodec.h",
